<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" ?>
<Patch>

  <!--
    ============================================================================
    Dryad body art switcher
    ============================================================================

    The eight dryad castes draw their body from the VANILLA PawnKindDef field
    PawnKindDef/lifeStages/li/bodyGraphicData/texPath, e.g.
        Things/Pawn/Animal/Dryad_Basic/Dryad_Basic
    which resolves to Textures/Things/Pawn/Animal/Dryad_Basic/Dryad_Basic_{east,north,south}.png

    This mod lets the player pick, per caste, between that modern art set and an
    "Old" set re-rooted from ExTextures/OLD/Animal_OLD into a real content path:
        Things/Pawn/Animal/OLD/Dryad_Basic/Dryad_Basic
    (ExTextures/ is not a RimWorld content root, so nothing inside it is loadable
    by a texPath. See Source/.../DryadSkin.cs for the full reasoning.)

    The switch itself happens in C#, not here. This patch only REPLACES the render
    node class of the Body node on the Animal render tree, so that our subclass gets
    consulted. The vanilla worker class is deliberately left alone, which keeps head
    offsets, useRottenColor, dessicated/rotting handling, layering, and the
    Wounds/Pack/Firefoam child nodes exactly as vanilla.

    Core tree reference:
      Data/Core/Defs/PawnRenderTreeDefs/PawnRenderTreeDefs.xml
        PawnRenderTreeDef defName="Animal"  -> root/children/li[tagDef="Body"]
  -->
  <Operation Class="PatchOperationReplace">
    <xpath>Defs/PawnRenderTreeDef[defName="Animal"]/root/children/li[tagDef="Body"]/nodeClass</xpath>
    <value>
      <nodeClass>HumanoidDryad.PawnRenderNode_DryadBody</nodeClass>
    </value>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
